-  ***** v373P (2026-10-20, dev_PS, OPT-IN, default OFF) -SceneryOwnPermutationOnly = GPULM_SCN_SELF_PERM=1 (lattice pre-pass + main pass).
-  A scenery receiver (owner O, permutation d of region r) already ignores O's other permutations of r as OCCLUDERS on every ray it casts (the
-  CPU's per-section override, mark 0x4A88DF; SOVR / scn_skip -- this mode changes nothing there). What it changes is the sun's PHOTON-RADIUS
-  CANDIDATE CULL (0x4A7068): the sun photons are cast against the default occluder state, i.e. against the UNION of O's permutations, so they
-  land on the outermost shell and a row beneath a sibling shell farther than the manager radius (0.5) from it is never a sun candidate. With the
-  switch such a row also probes the photons around the point where its sun ray leaves the sibling union (candidate = photon within r of P OR of S;
-  monotone, scenery rows only, rows without a sibling on the sun ray unchanged). It DIFFERS FROM THE CPU on purpose. Analytic / surface light
-  culls are not extended (the sun is the only photon-reach light on the test maps); the single-sun legacy path (-SunCullMultiOff) and -NoSunCull
-  ignore it. OFF = this script and fullgpu behave exactly as before.
