-  ***** v373C (2026-10-20, dev_CO, REPLACES the v373P/v373V behaviour under the SAME opt-in switch -SceneryOwnPermutationOnly; exe label "Scenery Multi
-  Permutation Fix (Experimental Improvement)"): CHOSEN-PERMUTATION SCENERY OCCLUDER. tool_fast bakes EVERY permutation section of a scenery object and
-  uses the UNION of all of them as the occluder for everything else, but the game draws ONE permutation per placement (the deterministic pick made at
-  object creation) -- so the shapes that are not drawn leave black splotches on the ground around the visible rock. With the switch:
-    * phase 1 (capture) installs a READ-ONLY hook at process_scenery_object 0x498962 (GPULM_CHOSEN_PERM=1, capture only) that records, per scenery
-      placement and region, the permutation the TOOL actually chose (the live object's chosen-permutation array, NOT an LCG replay) plus that
-      permutation's render-model sections -> $OUT\scenery_chosen_perm.bin (+ a text log scenery_chosen_perm.txt). Without the switch no hook is installed.
-    * fullgpu (GPULM_SCN_CHOSEN_PERM=1, lattice pre-pass AND main pass) removes every NON-chosen permutation section of a placement from the occluder
-      set of EVERY query: BSP texels, per-vertex rows, other scenery, the sun / sky / analytic / surface walks, the gather rays, the photon cast and the
-      r.e. photon-visibility blockers. A non-chosen section as a RECEIVER (all permutations are still baked, the tag format is unchanged) sees the
-      chosen-only world plus ITSELF (its own override-only instance) and still ignores its same-region siblings, exactly as the CPU's per-section override.
-      Placements with a variant, an unreadable array or a region without a chosen grid keep every permutation (logged).
-    * the v373V embedded-vertex fill is OFF in this mode (GPULM_SCN_EMBED_FIX=0 set here; the rock below the floor stays dark like the CPU), and the
-      v373P sun-candidate extension past sibling shells is not applied (no sibling shell is left in the photon world for a chosen section).
-  A capture made WITHOUT the switch has no scenery_chosen_perm.bin: fullgpu then REFUSES (exit 9) -- re-capture with the switch. OFF = this script, the
-  DLL and fullgpu behave exactly as before (no hook, no env, no file).
-  ***** v373H (2026-10-20, dev_CO, part of the SAME opt-in -- no extra switch) HIDDEN GROUND TEXEL FILL. A boulder sunk into the floor swallows the BSP
-  lightmap texels beneath it; their sample points lie INSIDE the drawn rock, so they come out black, are never seen, but bleed ~1 texel past the rock
-  silhouette through the bilinear filter ("black notches at the rock base"). fullgpu (host, in the compose, on the FINAL texel values) tests every BSP texel:
-  5 rays (+Z and four 12-degree tilts) from the texel's sample point (+0.001 along its normal); a ray votes iff its FIRST hit (structure + the ACTIVE,
-  i.e. chosen, scenery triangles) is a BACK face of a scenery triangle; >= 3 votes = HIDDEN (a rock floating above the ground gives a front-face first hit
-  and is not hidden). Hidden texels take the plain mean of their valid 8-neighbours in the chart grid, ring by ring (rgb, the direct/indirect split in
-  atlas_split.bin, the incident direction D and |D| in atlas_dir.bin all consistently). BSP texels only: scenery rows are untouched (the buried part of
-  the rock stays dark like the CPU), so does everything else. Side file in the run dir: hidden_texels.bin ('HDT1': ord, tix, first-hit owner, votes, ring,
-  0, pos xyz per hidden texel). GPULM_SCN_HIDDEN_FILL=0 (fullgpu env, A/B) turns just this off. DIFFERS FROM THE CPU on purpose. Single-pass maps only
-  (a chart is never split across parts, so the 8-neighbourhood is always in the same process).
-  ***** v373V2 (2026-10-20, dev_CO, part of the SAME opt-in -- no extra switch) NAMED-VARIANT OBJECTS BAKE WHAT THEY DRAW. process_scenery_object 0x498962 builds an
-  owner's section descriptors from variant 0's named regions (first permutation + damage states) and every permutation of the UNNAMED regions only, so a
-  placement with a named variant (h1\vehicles\lifepod "crashed": draws sections 3,4,2) got descriptors for the DEFAULT permutation's sections (0,1,2) -- the
-  drawn sections 3,4 had no occluder, no shading points and no lightmap records (-1 in the tag's section offsets; black in Sapien). With the switch the
-  DLL (GPULM_CHOSEN_PERM_ADD=1, set for EVERY tool run of the bake: the capture, the tag-writer skeleton, the phase-4 tool write-back) hooks 0x499072 (after both
-  descriptor loops) and, for each region, adds the sections of the CHOSEN permutation the same way the tool's own loop does (find by section -> else
-  scenery_occluder_insert + {region, 1<<lod, permbits 1, section}); already-enumerated sections are untouched, so objects that draw their default / first
-  permutation (the normal pod, every boulder) get the SAME descriptors as without it. Everything downstream is built by the tool from the descriptor vector.
-  The capture flags the placement's scenery_chosen_perm.bin record (flag 32), and fullgpu then trusts a VARIANT record (previously: all permutations stayed
-  occluders), so the non-chosen default sections (lifepod crashed: sec 0 and 1) leave the occluder set but stay baked as receivers. Log: "[GPULM chosenadd]"
-  lines per placement in the capture's gpulm.log and the skeleton run's gpulm.log. OFF = no byte is patched. The skeleton cache key carries "chosen_perm_add".
-  v373V2 crashfix (2026-10-20): the hook skips (and logs "section N NOT added") a chosen section the tool's own NUG-grid build could not use -- every drawable part foliage /
