-# ***** v322 BACK-FACE OPAQUE HITS EMIT NOTHING. Opaque geometry is TWO-SIDED (T[26], which is
-# (surface+104 != -1), is 0 for all 9,107 opaque triangles), so the traversal's back-face cull never
-# fires on it and radiance_opaque -- which looks radiance up by (surface,uv) with NO facing test --
-# hands a ray that landed INSIDE a closed shell that shell's lit OUTER radiance.
-# An independently written tracer (own Moller-Trumbore + BVH, validated bit-identical against brute
-# force over 819,200 rays, and matching our kernel's n_opaque on 99.5% of 16,000 queries) measured the
-# energy this contributes, and it is monotone in the CPU's own darkness:
-#     CPU-LIT 0.6% | CPU-dark 8.9% | worst dark decile 33.3% | the CPU's exact-zero set 95.3%
-# Measured effect of turning it on, against the v320 atlas (same capture, same seed):
-#     MAE dark      0.000704 -> 0.000629  (-10.6%)
-#     zero-set mean 0.000912 -> 0.000308  (-66.3%)   <- the CPU's own black texels
-#     dark ratio      1.6511 -> 1.5344 ;  floor 6.4726e-04 -> 5.5045e-04 (-15.0%)
-#     MAE lit       0.001817 -> 0.001819  (+0.07%, no regression) ; pearson 0.98649 -> 0.98660
-#     MAE covered   0.001530 -> 0.001497  (-2.2%)
-# NOTE this matches the CPU's OUTPUT, not a located divergence in its rules: T[26] mirrors the CPU's
-# own paired-surface test at intersect_static_surface 0x4B4507 exactly, so the CPU's traversal admits
-# these hits too and where its energy goes dark is still unlocated.
-# REQUIRES the v322 facing fix -- the old test dotted a WORLD direction against a LOCAL plane normal
-# across 187 non-identity instances and mis-classified hits 8.4x on lit texels; enabling this flag
-# WITHOUT that fix measured +0.83% MAE (worse), which is why it sat unshipped since v159.
-# v373BZ (2026-10-13, user: "yes promote backzero off"): DEFAULT OFF. The CPU has no facing test in its gather
-# (mc_final_gather 0x4B1A39 -> 0x4B29A2 -> 0x4A90CC -> 0x49C832 reads only surface,u,v); since the v372G faithful texel gate,
-# BACKZERO double-darkened. Guard sweep, un-floored: cyclotron +0.0028, high_10 +0.0089, earthcity_1 +0.0125, headlong +0.2413 pp.
-# -BackZero restores the old behaviour for A/B; -NoBackZero is kept (now the default) so old scripts still run.
