+<#
+  GPU LIGHTMAP BAKE -- one command, GPU-only lighting.
+
+  The CPU only loads the map and builds geometry/charts. Every lighting phase is severed
+  (photon cast, r.e. gather, mc_final_gather) and done on the GPU instead.
+
+    .\gpu_bake.ps1                       # cyclotron, the PRODUCT configuration (v359: super, gate THR 2, owner split,
+                                         #   rescue-all, seam lists when this capture has them, RNG-exact sun)
+    .\gpu_bake.ps1 -Quality low          # the old quick LOW bake
+    .\gpu_bake.ps1 -WriteBack            # also write the result back into the tool and save the tag
+    .\gpu_bake.ps1 -SkipCapture          # reuse the existing capture, re-bake only
+
+  Phases:  1 capture (CPU: load/geometry/charts, no lighting)   2 derive   3 GPU bake   [4 write-back]
+
+  ***** v359 PRODUCT DEFAULTS (int_v359, 2026-09-24). Every validated bake (V351..V358s, 99.66-99.68%) ran
+  `-Quality super -Gate -GateThr 2 -OwnerSplit` with GPULM_SEAM_LISTS=1 and GPULM_RESCUE_ALL=1 set by the RESEARCH
+  scripts, not by this script -- so a plain call baked something no one had validated. Those are now the defaults:
+    -Quality super, the v308 gate at THR 2 (-NoGate to disable; -Gate is accepted and changes nothing), the CPU owner
+    partition (-OwnerMerged for the old merged one; -OwnerSplit is accepted and changes nothing), GPULM_RESCUE_ALL=1
+    (-NoRescueAll), and seam lists AUTO: ON when this run dir holds a seam_lists.bin that belongs to this capture's
+    soup, otherwise BUILT from the capture's own soup_topo.bin (v360: CPU-exact -- 43,980/43,980 of the CPU's seam
+    records bit-identical on cyclotron; the fresh-capture bake scored 99.6674%).
+  The RNG-exact sun must be exact: a status other than EXACT / EXACT_UNVERIFIED (-SunScast) / SKIPPED throws unless
+  -AllowStochasticSun; -RequireExactSun makes SKIPPED throw too.
+
+  ***** v364 (2026-09-27) THE SUN'S PHOTON-RADIUS CULL is ON by default (+0.0557 pp on V362's inputs, 0.25 s): the CPU
+  evaluates the sun only where a first-bounce sun photon landed within r (0x4A7068), except on flag-0x40 receivers (the
+  skyline, 0x49B1FE). Phase 2 builds the flag-0x40 bypass table (bp_build.py) from a soup_flags.bin of THIS soup; without
+  one the cull is SKIPPED with a note (it never runs without the bypass: -2.60 pp). -NoSunCull turns it off (A/B);
+  -RequireSunCull throws instead of skipping.
+
+  ***** v366 TAG WRITER (2026-09-29) THE DIRECT TAG WRITER (v043-tagwriter): -WriteBackMode tool|direct|both.
+    tool   (default) the v363 phase 4, unchanged: the stock tool at GPULM_SEVER=3 saves the tags with this atlas injected.
+    direct a SKELETON tool run (dummy-lit, SEVER=3, ~1 min, in an isolated overlay $W\_gpulm_skel\wNN under a RENAMED
+           scenario; launched at phase-3 start alongside the GPU work; cached per capture) supplies the structure;
+           lm_tagwriter.py writes ltmp + truecolor + P8 (+ the scenario reference on a first bake) into $OUT\tagw_stage
+           (~27 s); lmw_validate.py --check-set gates it; with -WriteBack lmw_install.py backs up the live set
+           ($OUT\tag_backup_before_writeback + $W\_TAGBAK_auto\<ts>), writes the writeback_in_progress marker, replaces
+           file by file atomically and md5-verifies. Without -WriteBack it stops at the validated stage.
+    both   -WriteBack: the tool writes live as today, then the stage is A/B'd against it (lmw_validate.py --ab).
+
+  ***** v369 NEW-MAP GUARDS (guards12, 2026-10-03) so a map's FIRST bake (fresh capture) runs like cyclotron's:
+    1. the capture DLL writes soup_flags.bin itself (v043-suncull writer patch), so phase 2 builds the sun cull's flag-0x40
+       bypass table from THIS capture instead of needing a soup_flags_store entry; the DLL pre-flight requires the writer and
+       phase 1 checks its census line. The BSP is scanned for the DEBUG 'lightmap_cull' / 'lightmap_cull_pvs' markers
+       (parse_cluster_cull_markers 0x4B0522) -- NOT ported; a Note says so when present (cull_marker_check.py).
+    2. phase 3 refuses to start unless the v368 layered-walk inputs (tnrm.bin, tri_vpos/uv/mat/type, inst.bin, bitmaps) and the
+       v368o sky cell packet input (nug_planes.bin) are complete (pipeline_guard.py check walk / skycell), and it THROWS when
+       fullgpu stands a requested walk or the cell packet down instead of letting it fall back to the v367 behaviour.
+
+  ***** v369s (guard3, 2026-10-04) THE CPU'S FULL TWO-LEVEL RULE FOR INSTANCED GEOMETRY in the RNG-exact sky chain: an instanced
+  triangle is accepted at the FIRST root NUG cell that lists its instance (world AABB, sub_4B4A4C), whose cell-exit packet passes
+  its edges and whose inner walk on the OBJECT'S OWN NUG grid (sub_4B4941 -> 0x4B2DD4, build_nug_grid 0x4B3785) keeps its t;
+  winner = min (root cell, t). Phase 2 derives objgrids.bin (build_objgrids.py; its root rebuild must reproduce nug_planes.bin
